.TH CCOL_CHAN_RECV_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_recv_zc \- receive a message from the ccol_channel (it blocks)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_recv_zc(ccol_channel *ch, c_message_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
The function picks the correct queue itself. It uses the thread that calls
it:
- The owner thread receives from the ccol_workers_to_owner queue
- A worker thread receives from the ccol_owner_to_workers queue

The function blocks until a message arrives. Then it transfers the
ownership.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch          Channel to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message. It also gets the ownership of
            the data.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - The function received a message. The caller must free
                     target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args  - ch or target_buf is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function blocks until a message arrives in the chosen queue.
The function picks the direction itself from the ID of the thread.
The caller gets the ownership of target_buf->data and must free it.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_try_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_timed_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_send_zc (3)
